Package: openshell
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: NVIDIA OpenShell Maintainers <openshell@nvidia.com>
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Pre-Depends: init-system-helpers (>= 1.54~)
Homepage: https://github.com/NVIDIA/OpenShell
Description: Safe, sandboxed runtimes for autonomous AI agents
 OpenShell provides host-side command-line and gateway components for
 launching and managing policy-enforced AI agent sandboxes. The package
 installs the openshell CLI, standalone policy prover, openshell-gateway daemon,
 the VM compute driver helper, and the openshell-chutes-edge frontend, plus
 systemd units for running the gateway and the edge.
 .
 The gateway unit is user-scope (under /usr/lib/systemd/user/). To start
 it, run `systemctl --user enable --now openshell-gateway`.
 .
 The edge unit is system-scope and reads its Chutes API key from
 /etc/openshell/chutes-edge.env. After writing that file, run
 `systemctl enable --now openshell-chutes-edge`.
